obs A RED THIS LAP CAUSED AND CLOSED. rye_compile_reach went red naming mantra/snapshot_export_delivery.rye as carrying a runner's claim no build reaches -- because its census reads git ls-files over '*.rish', and the new hosted witness holding the build line was still untracked. git add closed it: asserted=0, verdict=ok. Same family as the baton's readme_metrics clause -- an instrument that counts the INDEX cannot see a file a lap has only written.
obs A RED THIS LAP CAUSED AND COULD NOT CLOSE, cited by stamp 20260910.180239 since REDS holds 40,311 of 40,960 and no row fits. My cold pass DIED at 284 lines rather than voiding -- tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh: line 1295: keeps: command not found. The cause is not the tree digest: sh STREAMS a script, so editing a running .sh in place makes the shell resume at a byte offset now holding different text, and it executes that text as a command. The word it tried to run, `keeps`, stands in a comment line I had inserted 1,822 bytes earlier in that same file.
obs PROVEN FROM THE FAILING SIDE IN A PEN before it was claimed: a victim .sh sleeping three seconds, edited mid-run by inserting 28 comment lines above the sleep, printed `ipt: command not found` -- a slice of the word `script` -- at a line number that is a comment in the file on disk. The sharper half is that the pen's victim then finished and exited 0. A corrupted run can look normal; the real runner merely happened to die loudly.
obs So `hold still while it runs` has a second reason nobody had written down. The digest reading -- tree_moved -- is the benign half, and four ships have reported it on today's card. The severe half is that the standing runner is a shell script the fleet edits, and a mid-run edit can make it execute arbitrary fragments of its own prose. The structural repair is for the runner to exec a snapshot of itself, which touches how every ship starts a pass and how the scan resolves its sibling beside $0 -- a design act on a shared surface, named rather than taken.
obs The cold reading is honestly LOST rather than void: a killed runner writes no run_verdict= line, and 238 green / 3 gated / 3 red at the moment of death is a partial. Of those three reds, one was mine and closed above, and two were the runner reporting on itself.
loom pass=standing_equipment_cold guards_green=238 gated=3 red=3 verdict=died_at_line_1295 cause=running_script_edited_in_place
